' ===================== RELATIONSHIPS =====================

' Inheritance - two node types
Node <|-- Sensor
Node <|-- OffloadableNode

' --- Association: a held reference / field in code ---
' OffloadManager keeps a reference to the nodes it manages (self.registry).
' It also CREATES the target via spawn_target(); creation shown by the method,
' not a second arrow, to keep one relationship per class pair.
OffloadManager "1" --> "0..*" OffloadableNode : manages > 

' --- Aggregation: OffloadableNode holds a StateSnapshot (self._snapshot) ---
' Hollow diamond (not composition): the snapshot is serialized and rebuilt on
' another machine, so it is not exclusively owned. 0..1 because it starts as
' None and only exists after get_snapshot() produces one.
OffloadableNode "1" o-- "0..1" StateSnapshot : produces >

' --- Data flow (ROS2 topic), NOT a stored reference ---
' Sensor publishes and OffloadableNode subscribes to /sensor/data. They are
' decoupled: neither holds a reference to the other's type. Shown as a dashed
' flow so the "sensor feeds node" path is visible without implying coupling.
Sensor ..> OffloadableNode : <<flow>> /sensor/data

' --- Association: NodeRecord is STORED as a field (self._registry) ---
OffloadManager "1" --> "0..*" NodeRecord : stores >

' --- Association: Migration is STORED as a field (self._active_migrations) ---
OffloadManager "1" --> "0..*" Migration : tracks >

' --- Dependency: created + returned by a method, NOT stored ---
OffloadManager ..> Decision : returns
OffloadableNode ..> NodeStatus : returns

note bottom of Migration
  "source" and "target" are ROLES here, per migration.
  They are NOT stored on OffloadableNode. Any node can
  be a source in one migration and a target in another.
  location is an open id (vehicle / edge / cloud / other DT).
end note

